      "text": "We have the system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n4u - 5v &= 23 \\tag{1} \\\\\n2u + 4v &= -8 \\tag{2}\n\\end{align*}\n\nTo eliminate one variable, we can multiply equation (2) by 2 to make the coefficients of $u$ in both equations equal:\n\\begin{align*}\n4u - 5v &= 23 \\tag{1} \\\\\n4u + 8v &= -16 \\tag{2'}\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we can subtract equation (1) from equation (2') to eliminate $u$:\n\\begin{align*}\n(4u + 8v) - (4u - 5v) &= -16 - 23 \\\\\n4u + 8v - 4u + 5v &= -39 \\\\\n13v &= -39 \\\\\nv &= -3\n\\end{align*}\n\nSubstituting $v = -3$ into equation (1), we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n4u - 5(-3) &= 23 \\\\\n4u + 15 &= 23 \\\\\n4u &= 8 \\\\\nu &= 2\n\\end{align*}\n\nFinally, we can find $u + v$:\n\\begin{align*}\nu + v &= 2 + (-3) \\\\\n&= -1\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo, the value of $u + v$ is $\\boxed{-1}$.",
