    "text": "We can solve the system of equations by adding the two equations together. This will eliminate the $v$ variable and allow us to solve for $u$.\n\n\\begin{align*}\n4u-5v &= 23 \\\\\n2u+4v &= -8 \\\\\n\\hline\n6u &= 15 \\\\\nu &= \\frac{15}{6} \\\\\nu &= \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow that we have the value of $u$, we can substitute it back into one of the original equations to solve for $v$.\n\n\\begin{align*}\n2u+4v &= -8 \\\\\n2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+4v &= -8 \\\\\n5+4v &= -8 \\\\\n4v &= -13 \\\\\nv &= -\\frac{13}{4}\n\\end{align*}\n\nFinally, we can find the value of $u+v$ by adding the values of $u$ and $v$.\n\n\\begin{align*}\nu+v &= \\frac{5}{2} + \\left(-\\frac{13}{4}\\right) \\\\\nu+v &= \\frac{10}{4} - \\frac{13}{4} \\\\\nu+v &= -\\frac{3}{4}\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the value of $u+v$ is $\\boxed{-\\frac{3}{4}}$.",
